  "question": {
    "text": "When a ball is dropped into a lake from a height <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> above the water level, it hits the water with a velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> and then sinks to the bottom with the constant velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>. It reaches the bottom of the lake <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></math> after it is dropped. The approximate depth of the lake is&nbsp;",
